# Read by ~/.claude/pre-push-checks/runner.sh before it runs its checks.
#
# Typecheck is OFF here, deliberately, and this is not laziness.
#
# The runner's typecheck is a raw `tsc -b`, which fails on any error. This repo
# carries 121 type errors inherited from before the 2026-09-12 hardening pass,
# so that check can never pass until every one of them is fixed, and a gate that
# always fails is a gate everyone learns to bypass with --no-verify. That is how
# this repo ended up with an unused oxlint config in the first place.
#
# The real gate is the ratchet: `npm run gate` fails only when the error count
# RISES against .quality-baseline.json, and it runs in CI on every push and PR
# (.github/workflows/ci.yml), alongside the build and both test suites, which
# must pass outright.
#
# Run it yourself before pushing:  npm run gate
PREPUSH_RUN_TYPECHECK=0
NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=4096
